  "content": "<div id=\"readability-page-1\" class=\"page\"><div id=\"\"> <p>APOD</p> <p>Astronomy Picture of the Day</p> <p> <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/archive/\">Discover the cosmos!</a> Each day a different image or photograph of our fascinating universe is featured, along with a brief explanation written by a professional astronomer. </p> <div><p><img width=\"925\" height=\"925\" src=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/content_mcgetchin_after.jpg?w=925&amp;h=925&amp;fit=clip&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint\" alt=\"An image of the lunar surface with a large depression at the center surrounded by raised ridges that slope down back to the surface.\" decoding=\"async\" srcset=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/content_mcgetchin_after.jpg?w=925&amp;h=925&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 925w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/content_mcgetchin_after.jpg?w=150&amp;h=150&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 150w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/content_mcgetchin_after.jpg?w=300&amp;h=300&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 300w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/content_mcgetchin_after.jpg?w=768&amp;h=768&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 768w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/content_mcgetchin_after.jpg?w=50&amp;h=50&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 50w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/content_mcgetchin_after.jpg?w=100&amp;h=100&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 100w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/content_mcgetchin_after.jpg?w=200&amp;h=200&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 200w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/content_mcgetchin_after.jpg?w=400&amp;h=400&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 400w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/content_mcgetchin_after.jpg?w=600&amp;h=600&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 600w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/content_mcgetchin_after.jpg?w=900&amp;h=900&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 900w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 925px) 100vw, 925px\"><img width=\"925\" height=\"925\" src=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/content_mcgetchin_before.jpg?w=925&amp;h=925&amp;fit=clip&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint\" alt=\"An image of the lunar surface speckled wth impressions (craters) of various small sizes.\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/content_mcgetchin_before.jpg?w=925&amp;h=925&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 925w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/content_mcgetchin_before.jpg?w=150&amp;h=150&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 150w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/content_mcgetchin_before.jpg?w=300&amp;h=300&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 300w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/content_mcgetchin_before.jpg?w=768&amp;h=768&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 768w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/content_mcgetchin_before.jpg?w=50&amp;h=50&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 50w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/content_mcgetchin_before.jpg?w=100&amp;h=100&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 100w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/content_mcgetchin_before.jpg?w=200&amp;h=200&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 200w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/content_mcgetchin_before.jpg?w=400&amp;h=400&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 400w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/content_mcgetchin_before.jpg?w=600&amp;h=600&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 600w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/content_mcgetchin_before.jpg?w=900&amp;h=900&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 900w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 925px) 100vw, 925px\"></p></div> <div> <div> <p><strong>Explanation:</strong> A once-in-a-lifetime crater has appeared on the Moon! A comet or asteroid roughly the size of a <a href=\"https://www.fisheries.noaa.gov/species/humpback-whale\">humpback whale</a> (approximately 10-20 meters, 30-60 feet) crashed into the Moon sometime between April and May of 2024. The <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/lro/\">Lunar Reconnaissance Orbiter</a> (LRO), with its <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/image-article/apod-2024-june-2-rotating-moon-from-lro/\">monthly monitoring of the Moon</a>, captured <a href=\"https://lroc.im-ldi.com/images/1501\">today’s images</a> of the lunar surface before and after the event. The resulting crater, named after Apollo-era lunar scientist <a href=\"https://rock.geosociety.org/net/documents/gsa/memorials/v16/McGetchin-TR.pdf\">McGetchin</a>, is two soccer fields across. Craters of this size are only expected once <a href=\"https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2001SSRv...96...55N/abstract\">every 132 years</a>! <a href=\"https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/sciadv.aeh9568\">Follow up thermal imaging</a> revealed a <a href=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/content/dam/science/missions/lro/McGetchinLROblinkImage.gif\">large cold spot</a> that surrounds the warm crater. Surface impacts will puff up the loose lunar sediment, or <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/biological-physical/what-is-lunar-regolith/\">regolith</a>, making it less dense and harder to retain heat. This event affected an area <a href=\"https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/sciadv.aeh7812\">much larger than the visible crater</a>, which will inform humanity’s understanding of surface impacts and the evolution of the Moon’s surface. It also reminds us all to be <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/image-article/apod-2025-august-3-milky-way-and-exploding-meteor/\">thankful for Earth's atmosphere</a>.</p><p><strong>APOD's submission email has changed.</strong> Please see <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/submit/\">APOD Submissions.</a><br><strong>APOD's main NASA site is <a href=\"https://asterisk.apod.com/viewtopic.php?t=45023\">moving</a>:</strong> From <a href=\"https://apod.nasa.gov/\">apod.nasa.gov</a> to <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod\">science.nasa.gov/apod</a><br><strong>Tomorrow's picture:</strong> the great unknown </p></div> <div> <table> <tbody> <tr> <th scope=\"row\">Date:</th> <td> September 23, 2026 </td> </tr> <tr> <th scope=\"row\">Credit:</th> <td> NASA/GSFC/Intuitive Machines </td> </tr> <tr> <th scope=\"row\">Authors &amp; editors:</th> <td> Keighley Rockcliffe, Robert Nemiroff, Jerry Bonnell, Cecilia Chirenti </td> </tr> <tr> <th scope=\"row\">A service of:</th> <td> <a href=\"https://science.gsfc.nasa.gov/astrophysics/\" target=\"_blank\">ASD</a> at <a href=\"https://www.nasa.gov/\" target=\"_blank\">NASA</a> / <a href=\"https://www.nasa.gov/centers/goddard/\" target=\"_blank\">GSFC</a>,<br><a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/learn/about-science-activation/\" target=\"_blank\">NASA Science Activation</a> &amp; <a href=\"https://www.mtu.edu/\" target=\"_blank\">Michigan Tech. U.</a> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> </div> </div></div>",
